<figure class="parser-map" aria-labelledby="parser-map-title">
  <figcaption id="parser-map-title"><span>STATE MACHINE</span><strong>State survives when an escape sequence is split anywhere</strong></figcaption>
  <div class="parser-map__states"><div class="active"><b>ground</b><span>print / execute</span></div><i>ESC</i><div><b>escape</b><span>wait for introducer</span></div><i>[</i><div><b>CSI</b><span>collect digits</span></div><i>m</i><div class="active"><b>ground</b><span>emit SGR</span></div></div>
  <div class="parser-map__chunks"><code>… 1B</code><code>5B 33</code><code>32 6D …</code><span>three independent reads → one <strong>SGR 32</strong> action</span></div>
  <p>The parser consumes a byte stream, not messages. Ending a call in <code>escape</code> or <code>CSI</code> is normal; the next call resumes that state.</p>
</figure>
